# ============================================================================
# This file is assembled from the GitHub gitignore templates
# (https://github.com/github/gitignore):
#
#   Node.gitignore, the primary template for this project
#   Global/macOS.gitignore, contributors are not all on Linux
#   Global/Linux.gitignore
#   Global/Windows.gitignore
#   Global/VisualStudioCode.gitignore
#
# There is no Chrome-extension template, so the extension-specific entries are
# written here by hand, at the end.
#
# Project-specific entries come first because they are the ones that matter and
# the reason this repository has an unusual arrangement. A generic list would
# hide that; these are the lines someone should read before adding to it.
# ============================================================================

# --- Project: never committed ------------------------------------------------

# Local notes and working documents. All of docs/ is private: planning,
# preferences, roadmap thinking. Nothing under it belongs in the repository.
# (docs/PLAN.md and the private notes were both committed by mistake and had to
# be purged from history.)
docs/

# Real YouTube captures. tools/capture.mjs is the only thing that writes these,
# and the only thing in the project that opens youtube.com. A raw capture
# contains signed caption URLs (signature, ei, ip, expire), which are session
# artifacts rather than fixtures. Capture is a local setup step:
# `npm run capture -- <videoId>`.
test/fixtures/

# Partial captures from a run that failed mid-collection. Kept on disk so a spent
# open still yields evidence, never as a fixture, derive-synthetic refuses them.
test/fixtures/*.partial/

# Generated MKV test fixtures for the container parser, real containers written
# by `ffmpeg`, rebuilt in two seconds by `npm run fixtures`.
#
# A SEPARATE directory from test/fixtures/ on purpose, because the two are
# gitignored for different reasons and only one is reproducible:
#   test/fixtures/  real captures, ignored because a capture carries a signed URL
#   test/mkv/       generated, ignored because generating is cheaper than storing
# Collapsing them would hide that difference.
test/mkv/*.mkv

# The Matroska conformance suite, a DEVELOPMENT dependency, not a test fixture.
# Real films (Big Buck Bunny, Elephants Dream), CC-BY, hundreds of megabytes, so
# they are downloaded rather than committed: `npm run conformance:fetch`.
#
# Fetched over the network and not reproducible, which makes it a third kind of
# ignored directory again. Nothing in `src/` reads these and they are never
# packaged.
#
# The runner lives in test/conformance/ so the top-level runner does not scan it,
# a contributor without the files must still be able to run `npm test`.
test/conformance/*.mkv

