# Built Visual Studio Code Extensions
*.vsix

# ============================================================================
# Chrome extension, written by hand.
#
# There is no extension template in the github/gitignore repository, so these are
# ours. This project has no build step: the extension is loaded unpacked straight
# from the repository, so what would normally be build artefacts are simply not
# produced. Noted rather than silently omitted, because a reader who expects a
# `dist/` here should know why there is none.
# ============================================================================

# Packed extension archives and signing keys. A .zip of the unpacked extension is
# the usual way to sideload or to prepare a Web Store upload, and a .pem is the
# private key behind a .crx. None of these belongs in git, and none appears in the
# Node template, so the Node section above does not already cover them.
*.zip
*.crx
*.pem

# --- Local agent tooling -----------------------------------------------------
#
# The directories below are written by whichever AI coding tools a developer
# happens to run, each keeping its own `.X/skills/` copy of the same generated
# content. They are per-developer tool state, not project content: they are not
# authored here, they differ by which tools are installed, and six identical
# copies of one skill tree is not something to commit.
#
# If a shared agent configuration is ever wanted, commit it explicitly with
# `git add -f` and delete the corresponding line here.
.agent/
.agents/
.claude/
.cline/
.cursor/
.pi/


# VS Code workspace file: local folder paths, not shared config.
*.code-workspace

# Build output: the staged set and the store ZIP. Reproducible from source.
build/

# Screenshots written by the preview capture scripts, for visual review. They are
# regenerated on demand and are large; the review itself is not a source artifact.
tools/ui/assets/
